1
00:00:13,000 --> 00:00:15,860
Welcome to the Breath Reset.

2
00:00:15,920 --> 00:00:18,810
Today we're going to
practice Breathe Light,

3
00:00:18,860 --> 00:00:23,680
learning to breathe a little
quieter, softer, and more comfortably.

4
00:00:24,100 --> 00:00:26,830
We'll measure our BOLT
score before and after,

5
00:00:26,880 --> 00:00:29,520
just to notice whether anything changes.

6
00:00:29,720 --> 00:00:31,000
Let's begin.

7
00:00:31,980 --> 00:00:35,840
Take a few natural
breaths through your nose.

8
00:00:37,620 --> 00:00:40,030
On my cue, you're going to be taking

9
00:00:40,080 --> 00:00:43,170
one more inhale, and after the exhale,

10
00:00:43,220 --> 00:00:47,760
I want you to pinch your nose, and
the timer will start on the screen.

11
00:00:48,420 --> 00:00:54,220
Stop at the first clear urge to
breathe, then return to normal breathing.

12
00:00:55,280 --> 00:01:02,340
Ready? Inhale. Exhale. And begin.

13
00:02:02,890 --> 00:02:05,670
Now make a note of your score,

14
00:02:05,870 --> 00:02:10,370
and allow your breathing to
return completely to normal.

15
00:02:12,680 --> 00:02:17,710
Gently close your eyes and allow your

16
00:02:17,760 --> 00:02:22,140
sit bones to feel grounded beneath you.

17
00:02:22,760 --> 00:02:29,460
Imagine a piece of string lightly
lifting you from the crown of your head.

18
00:02:30,680 --> 00:02:34,290
Let your shoulders
soften and relax your jaw

19
00:02:34,340 --> 00:02:41,900
and begin by simply
noticing your breathing.

20
00:02:43,060 --> 00:02:47,550
Notice the air entering through
the nose, perhaps feeling

21
00:02:47,600 --> 00:02:53,540
slightly cooler as it comes in
and a little warmer as it leaves.

22
00:02:54,420 --> 00:02:59,360
No need to change
anything yet, just notice.

23
00:03:06,460 --> 00:03:11,300
Now begin to bring a little
softness into your breathing.

24
00:03:11,500 --> 00:03:17,990
Allow the inhale to
become gentle and quiet and

25
00:03:18,040 --> 00:03:22,800
as you exhale simply
allow the air to leave.

26
00:03:24,490 --> 00:03:28,270
No pushing, no forcing.

27
00:03:32,250 --> 00:03:35,920
With your next breath
see if you can make the

28
00:03:35,970 --> 00:03:43,070
inhale just a little
smaller, a little softer.

29
00:03:44,200 --> 00:03:47,890
And allow the exhale to happen naturally.

30
00:03:50,280 --> 00:03:52,150
Imagine there's a delicate feather

31
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:55,170
resting just beneath your nose and as you

32
00:03:55,220 --> 00:03:59,590
breathe in and out see if you can breathe

33
00:03:59,640 --> 00:04:04,900
so gently that the feather barely moves.

34
00:04:05,160 --> 00:04:08,850
That's the quality we're looking for.

35
00:04:08,900 --> 00:04:14,440
Soft, quiet, imperceptible breathing.

36
00:04:24,940 --> 00:04:30,940
Now we're going to experiment
with breathing a little less air.

37
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:35,150
Not necessarily breathing
slower but taking

38
00:04:35,200 --> 00:04:38,870
in a smaller amount of
air with each breath.

39
00:04:41,110 --> 00:04:47,880
Soften the inhale, relax
the exhale and then see if

40
00:04:47,930 --> 00:04:53,350
you can soften the next
inhale just a little more.

41
00:04:59,310 --> 00:05:02,200
As you reduce the amount of air you're

42
00:05:02,250 --> 00:05:06,220
breathing you may begin
to notice a very slight

43
00:05:06,270 --> 00:05:11,800
desire to take a big
breath, a gentle feeling

44
00:05:11,850 --> 00:05:15,670
that you could do with
just a little more air.

45
00:05:16,030 --> 00:05:23,450
That's what we're exploring,
just a mild comfortable sensation.

46
00:05:32,870 --> 00:05:36,880
Continue breathing
gently through your nose,

47
00:05:36,930 --> 00:05:43,690
a soft inhale and an effortless exhale.

48
00:05:43,930 --> 00:05:49,680
Notice whether you can make your
breathing just a little lighter,

49
00:05:49,730 --> 00:05:54,230
almost as though you're breathing
less air than you normally would.

50
00:05:59,910 --> 00:06:04,460
And remember you don't need
to achieve anything here,

51
00:06:04,510 --> 00:06:08,390
just stay curious about what you notice.

52
00:06:14,710 --> 00:06:20,930
And now slowly release any
control over your breathing.

53
00:06:21,350 --> 00:06:26,070
Allow your body to breathe in
whatever rhythm feels natural.

54
00:06:26,810 --> 00:06:31,330
No need to make the breath
smaller or slower anymore.

55
00:06:36,310 --> 00:06:39,150
Notice how you're feeling.

56
00:06:39,430 --> 00:06:42,030
Does your breathing feel any different?

57
00:06:42,870 --> 00:06:46,300
Perhaps a little quieter or more relaxed

58
00:06:46,350 --> 00:06:50,990
or perhaps it feels exactly the same.

59
00:06:51,390 --> 00:06:54,010
Whatever you notice is okay.

60
00:06:57,470 --> 00:07:04,670
When you're ready, gently bring
your awareness back into the room.

61
00:07:08,940 --> 00:07:11,890
Now we're going to repeat
our BOLT measurement.

62
00:07:11,940 --> 00:07:15,360
Take a few normal breaths.

63
00:07:15,560 --> 00:07:20,330
On my cue, we're going to
be taking one more inhale,

64
00:07:20,380 --> 00:07:24,920
and exhale, then gently pinch
our nose and watch the timer.

65
00:07:25,520 --> 00:07:29,000
Stop at the first clear urge to breathe,

66
00:07:29,600 --> 00:07:32,780
then release and return
to normal breathing.

67
00:07:33,780 --> 00:07:40,920
Take a nice big inhale, exhale, and begin.

68
00:08:41,760 --> 00:08:44,540
Now make a note of your second score.

69
00:08:44,800 --> 00:08:48,600
Was it higher, lower, or about the same?

70
00:08:52,120 --> 00:08:55,090
Remember, the goal isn't to
achieve a particular number.

71
00:08:55,140 --> 00:08:58,110
It's to become more aware
of your breathing and

72
00:08:58,160 --> 00:09:01,420
learn how to make it
comfortable and efficient.

73
00:09:01,920 --> 00:09:04,170
As you go through your day, notice whether

74
00:09:04,220 --> 00:09:06,710
you're breathing with
more effort than you need.

75
00:09:06,760 --> 00:09:09,270
And if it feels comfortable,
allow it to soften.

76
00:09:09,320 --> 00:09:14,500
Sometimes breathing better
is simply about doing less.

